# Tells Cloudflare's Wrangler which files NOT to publish as public static
# assets, even though they live in this same repo. Same syntax as
# .gitignore -- this only affects what gets deployed to the live site, it
# has no effect on git itself.
#
# Why each of these is here:
#   source/               - master.xlsx is your private data source, and at
#                            33+ MiB it's also well over Cloudflare's 25 MiB
#                            per-file limit for a published asset. This was
#                            the exact cause of every deployment failing
#                            silently since FY23-24 was added.
#   .git                  - Wrangler walks the real filesystem, which
#                            includes git's own history folder -- this can
#                            contain older, equally oversized copies of
#                            master.xlsx from past commits, and should never
#                            be public regardless of size (it's your full
#                            commit history).
#   access/roles.csv            - lists real email addresses per person/role.
#   access/cloudflare-policies.md - same: real emails, auto-generated from roles.csv.
#   scripts/, .github/, README.md - internal tooling and docs, not meant to
#                            be part of the served site.
#   .wrangler, node_modules, .DS_Store - build/OS artifacts, never useful public.

.git
.wrangler
node_modules
.DS_Store
source/
scripts/
access/roles.csv
access/cloudflare-policies.md
.github/
README.md
